{
  "header": [
    "PROPOSAL — the theme map `molo content curate` uses to choose words.",
    "An editor is expected to read this file and correct it. It is data, not code:",
    "editing a list here changes which words land in which skill, with no rebuild.",
    "",
    "There is deliberately no model call anywhere in this matching. Every word a",
    "skill gets can be traced to one line of this file, which is the point.",
    "",
    "HOW A WORD REACHES A SKILL",
    "",
    "  1. `exclude` wins over everything. If any English gloss on the word contains",
    "     an excluded phrase, the theme refuses it. This is how the lexicon's",
    "     statistics and medical terminology are kept out of a beginner course.",
    "  2. `senses` is the strongest evidence, worth 3. These match the `sense`",
    "     attribute the Gothenburg corpus puts on a token: the corpus is telling us",
    "     what the word meant in an actual conversation, which beats anything we",
    "     could infer from a dictionary gloss.",
    "  3. `keywords` is worth 2 and matches whole words or whole phrases inside an",
    "     English gloss, so `car` does not match `carry` and `ear` does not match",
    "     `year`.",
    "  4. `lemmaPatterns` is worth 1, the weakest, and matches the isiXhosa lemma",
    "     itself. Only the pronunciation theme uses it, because 'contains a click",
    "     letter' is a fact about spelling and no gloss could express it. Spelling",
    "     is weakest so a click word that some other theme can claim on meaning goes",
    "     there instead, and the click drill gets what is left.",
    "  5. `pos`, when present, restricts the theme to those parts of speech.",
    "  6. `maxLemmaWords`, when present, refuses a lemma of more words than that",
    "     (split on spaces and slashes). The click theme takes single words only:",
    "     a hospital department's name is not a beginner's example of a click.",
    "     `molo content reconcile-unit-1` applies the same refusals to exercises",
    "     already written, so a word taken out is never chosen again.",
    "",
    "A word goes to the theme with the most evidence; a tie goes to whichever skill",
    "comes first in `spine.json`, so a word is taught the first time it is useful",
    "and never twice.",
    "",
    "SITUATIONS, NOT VOCABULARY FIELDS",
    "",
    "The themes follow the units, and the units are situations, so verbs sit with",
    "the situation that needs them: `funa`, `thanda` and `cela` belong to ordering",
    "food, not to a verb list. That is why `wanting`, `cooking`, `transport` and",
    "`help-trouble` carry verb keywords rather than leaving every verb to a grammar",
    "skill.",
    "",
    "KNOWN WEAKNESSES, for whoever revises this",
    "",
    "  - The glosses come from isixhosa.click and are uneven: some are one word,",
    "    some are a sentence. Keywords match the uneven ones badly.",
    "  - The lexicon carries a large tail of statistical, legal and medical",
    "    terminology from its other users. The `exclude` lists here catch the worst",
    "    of it and will not catch all of it.",
    "  - Nothing here knows register. A word can match `food` perfectly and still be",
    "    the wrong word to teach a visitor; that judgement is the editor's."
  ],
