    "clicks": {
      "note": "Words carrying a click, chosen for the sound and not the meaning. c is dental, x lateral, q palatal; the aspirated and nasalised variants (ch, xh, qh, nc, nx, nq, gc, gx, gq) are the same three places of articulation. In isiXhosa orthography c, x and q are always clicks, so the pattern is simply 'contains one'. Everything matched is a real lexicon word: no minimal pair is invented.",
